{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/init()"],"anchor":"Creating-a-Command-Buffer","title":"Creating a Command Buffer"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/count","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/isEmpty"],"anchor":"Inspecting-a-Command-Buffer","title":"Inspecting a Command Buffer"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/clone(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(from:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/despawn(_:)"],"anchor":"Spawning-and-Despawning-Entities","title":"Spawning and Despawning Entities"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/insert(_:into:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/remove(_:from:)"],"anchor":"Adding-and-Removing-Components","title":"Adding and Removing Components"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/addChild(_:to:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:childOf:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/removeParent(of:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/relate(_:_:to:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/unrelate(_:_:from:)"],"anchor":"Changing-the-Hierarchy-and-Relations","title":"Changing the Hierarchy and Relations"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/send(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/trigger(_:on:)"],"anchor":"Sending-Events","title":"Sending Events"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/insert(resource:)"],"anchor":"Changing-Resources","title":"Changing Resources"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/record(_:)"],"anchor":"Recording-Any-Change","title":"Recording Any Change"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/DisablingEntitiesAndUsingPrefabs","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryingAWorld","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/RelatingEntities"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a query or an update visits a world’s entities, the world can’t be changed in other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ways: spawning or despawning an entity, or adding or removing a component, would disturb the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage being visited. Record such changes in a command buffer instead, and apply them with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" once the visit is over. The following example despawns every entity whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"health has run out:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Health(current: 0))","world.spawn(Health(current: 10))","","var commands = Commands()","for (entity, health) in world.query(Health.self) where health.current <= 0 {","    commands.despawn(entity)","}","world.apply(commands)","","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A command on an entity that is no longer live when it applies does nothing, so two commands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that despawn the same entity are safe."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Naming-Entities-That-Commands-Will-Spawn","text":"Naming Entities That Commands Will Spawn","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" returns a placeholder handle for the entity it will create. Later commands in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same buffer can name that placeholder, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" returns the real handles of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entities it spawned, in the order their commands were recorded:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","var commands = Commands()","let ship = commands.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","let turret = commands.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 0))","commands.addChild(turret, to: ship)","","let spawned = world.apply(commands)","print(world.parent(of: spawned[1]) == spawned[0])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A placeholder stands for its entity only inside the buffer that returned it; the world holds no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entity with that handle.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Commands-from-Systems","text":"Commands from Systems","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system running alongside others can’t apply commands itself, because applying them would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change entities the other systems are reading. It queues them with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead, and the schedule applies every queued buffer at the end of each wave of systems."}]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands"},"metadata":{"title":"Commands","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:11WorldModule8CommandsV","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Commands.swift#L55","fileName":"Commands.swift"}},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/commands"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A buffer of changes to a world, recorded now and applied later in the order they were"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recorded."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Commands/addChild(_:to:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/commands\/addchild(_:to:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Records making one entity the last child of another, as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/addChild(_:to:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/addChild(_:to:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"addChild","kind":"identifier"},{"text"